===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|twerc|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|twerc|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|dwergaz|lang=de}}. The apparent "double consonant shift", in which Middle High German t shifted to z, is irregular and very unusual, but an even more extreme "triple shift" can be seen in {{term|zwingen|lang=de}}.

